r suites, never counts.\n        - If no tests passed or failed, write [] for those fields.\n        - Never exit without writing the result contract first.\n        - After writing the result contract, print a short human summary.\n\n        Codex approval note:\n        Approved after Codex review. Keep scope to server-side start guard plus calm walker blocked state; if the server error needs a non-generic walker message, handle it inside WalkerDashboardClient without widening file scope.\n\n        Approved preflight follows verbatim:\n\n        {\n  \"id\": \"TASK-0201-PRICE-ENFORCEMENT-START-BLOCK\",\n  \"status\": \"ready_for_approval\",\n  \"phase\": \"preflight\",\n  \"summary\": \"Block walk start when dogWalkers.currentPrice is null or '0.00'. Enforcement at two layers: (1) server action in walksRepo.startWalk() \\u2014 extend the existing assignment query to also fetch currentPrice and throw 'Price not set' before inserting the walk row; (2) UI in WalkerDashboardClient.tsx \\u2014 replace the start button with a calm inline notice when the dog's currentPrice is '0.00' or empty. No new files needed. All touched files are within the allowlist.\",\n  \"files_to_touch\": [\n    \"src/lib/repositories/walksRepo.ts\",\n    \"src/app/walker/dashboard/WalkerDashboardClient.tsx\"\n  ],\n  \"commands_to_run\": [\n    \"npx tsc --noEmit\",\n    \"npx eslint src/lib/repositories/walksRepo.ts src/app/walker/dashboard/WalkerDashboardClient.tsx\"\n  ],\n  \"validation_plan\": [\n    \"TypeScript: npx tsc --noEmit \\u2014 expect zero new errors\",\n    \"Lint: eslint on both touched files \\u2014 expect zero new warnings\",\n    \"Manual (server guard): with a dog assigned at price 0.00, call startWalkAction \\u2014 expect thrown error 'Price not set' and no walk row inserted in DB\",\n    \"Manual (UI guard): load walker dashboard with a 0.00-price dog \\u2014 expect start button replaced by inline notice, no start possible without JS bypass\",\n    \"Manual (happy path